      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/download-reaches-the-browser"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "Both download controllers resolve the object BEFORE any header is sent -- DocumentStorage reports a missing object through a typed exception rather than a bare RuntimeException raised from inside the streamDownload callback, where the status line has already been decided and the observed code is an accident of when the exception surfaces relative to the header flush. Each route answers a deliberate status with a body and a log line naming the object key, so an operator can tell 'object storage is missing this object' from 'doccum crashed'. A test deletes the faked object behind a live row and asserts the status, the message and the log entry, for the current-version route and the per-version route both; the chosen status is stated in the docblock with its reasoning. The presigned path answers MinIO's own 404 and is left as is, noted rather than fixed. This matters because /data is the only volume and the backup story is 'copy /data': a restore that brings the database but not objects/ is the likeliest operator mistake in the product, and item/self-hosting-docs must be able to say what happens then.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T03:35:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T03:53:32Z",
      "result": [
