    {
      "@id": "item/ledger-mutation-nodes",
      "@type": "Action",
      "order": 31,
      "name": "Mutation runs become ledger nodes with verdicts, so a prediction cannot pass as a finding",
      "url": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/issues/150",
      "isBasedOn": [
        "spec:13-infrastructure"
      ],
      "size": "S",
      "release": "v1.0.0",
      "dependsOn": [
        "item/trash-view"
      ],
      "doneWhen": "A Mutation node type exists on the Ledger, sibling to pullRequests and decisions, carrying implements, pullRequest, run, headSha, mutant (what was broken), check (the named assertion that must trip) and verdict, one of negative (the check went red -- the good outcome), positive (the guard is not load-bearing) or void (the run died before reaching the assertion, so it is evidence of nothing). LedgerValidator enforces three rules: a Completed item based on spec:10 must be implements-referenced by at least one negative Mutation with a non-empty check; a positive or void Mutation blocks its item's Completion until a later one supersedes it; and check is required on a negative verdict, because a failure that names no assertion is not evidence. Decision gains an evidence term referencing Mutation nodes, so a decision claiming a guard is load-bearing either cites a run or visibly does not -- and the absence is the signal, no rule needed. PullRequest gains mainRunUrl and mainConclusion, and a Run may not reach outcome completed while a PR merged in it lacks mainConclusion, which makes LOOP step 3's claim about main's ref a recorded fact rather than a habit. The historical mutation PRs are back-filled with verdicts read from their workflow runs -- NINE of them (118, 122, 130, 132, 141, 145, 148, 149, 154), yielding ten nodes because #148 ran twice; the clause said \"six\" and then listed eight, which was my miscount when I wrote it, and #154 postdates the text. Corrected here at completion rather than quietly, because a count nobody checked is how the void run in that very list nearly passed for proof; existing PR node names are left alone, because history is append-only. The 39 mechanical entries in mutations.json get no nodes: mutation-check.php re-proves them every CI run, so their evidence is the green tests run itself.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
      "startTime": "2026-09-18T04:00:00Z",
      "endTime": "2026-09-18T04:35:56Z",
      "result": [
        "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/156"
      ]
    },
