      "doneWhen": "Login resolves an identifier that is either a username or an email through AuthenticateUser, which today compares by email alone; the collision rule is decided and stated -- and the decision, recorded at completion rather than by quietly dropping the clause, is that the case this parenthetical describes (a value that is a valid username AND some other account's email) is UNREACHABLE by construction: usernameRules() excludes @ and an email must contain one. No precedence rule was invented for it, because inventing one would assert an ambiguity that does not exist and the next reader would reason from it. What the clause was standing on was enforced instead -- see decision/0042 and User::booted(); login.blade.php stops using type=\"email\" on the identifier field, which rejects a username in the browser before any of this is reached; tests cover login by each, and the docblock claim in AuthenticateUser that this is 'tracked as its own item' becomes true.",
