      ],
      "doneWhen": "item/spec-reconcile made section 8 the section section 2, section 13, section 14 and section 16 all defer to -- and section 8 itself still describes a system that was never built. Each verified against the repository, not inferred: its projection table uses searchable_type/searchable_id where searchable_type appears in ZERO migrations and subject_type appears in TWO; it describes a Scout Searchable trait, toSearchableArray(), #[SearchUsingFullText] and a Scout query() callback where NO Scout Searchable trait exists anywhere in app/ and filtering happens in Services\\Search and SearchIndex::search(); and its seam table lists TsvectorSearchIndex for PostgreSQL where app/Search/ contains only Fts5SearchIndex and LikeSearchIndex. Found while reconciling and deliberately left out of that diff, because decision/0077's standard is that a spec edit stays small, reviewable and doc-only, and widening the branch would be the auditor-edits-its-own-standard problem in miniature. THIS IS A DEPENDENCY OF item/v1-audit, not a nicety: decision/0084 made the audit depend on item/spec-reconcile specifically so it measures against a corrected spec. If section 8 is still partly false when the audit runs, the reconciliation manufactures the false confidence it was meant to remove -- the audit would check the product against implementation detail for a library this project does not use. Done when every section 8 claim is either true of the shipped code or explicitly marked superseded with a pointer, on item/spec-reconcile's terms: column names match the migration and the model; the Scout mechanics are replaced by what Services\\Search and SearchIndex actually do; the TsvectorSearchIndex row is marked unbuilt with a pointer to item/tsvector-index rather than presented as shipped; a revisions-note entry records the pass; the heading set stays BYTE-IDENTICAL (grep '^#' then diff, since LedgerValidator's spec-anchor rule slugs heading text); and the validator passes. There is no test for prose, and the validator proves only that no anchor broke -- not that the text is true. The check on the text is that it stays a small, reviewable, doc-only diff.",
      "actionStatus": "CompletedActionStatus",
