      "mutant": "Removed only the `wire:click=\"saveRole({{ $role->id }})\"` attribute from the Save button in resources/views/livewire/admin/roles.blade.php. The button still renders, still carries its data-test, and is still clickable -- it simply no longer reaches the component. Chosen because it is invisible to every other job: App\\Livewire\\Admin\\Roles::saveRole() is untouched, so AdminRolesTest, which calls that method directly through Livewire's test harness, stays green, as do guards, lint and all six test matrix jobs.",
      "check": "container-smoke.mjs checkAdminRolesPage() -- the image job failed at the named assertion \"member role never gained periods.manage through the real form\", dumping \"toggling periods.manage for the member role through /admin/roles never reached the database -- raw output: HOLDS:no\". Not a locator timeout on the way there: the log shows the check opened /admin/roles, found the member row, found the periods.manage checkbox, confirmed it started unchecked, ticked it and clicked Save. Only the database failed to move, which is what a Save button that no longer reaches its component looks like from outside. The other twelve checks on the same run all passed -- guards, lint, build assets, composer audit, dependency review, validate ledger and all six test matrix jobs -- which is the other half of the evidence: AdminRolesTest calls saveRole() directly through Livewire's test harness and cannot see this defect at all. Run https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35329472286.",
