      "headSha": "1b576c0e3f41d571b5ca63d5604fda7c1d1dcc44",
      "mutant": "Built the smoke image with DOCCUM_VERSION=9.9.9, so org.opencontainers.image.version reads 9.9.9, while starting the container with -e DOCCUM_VERSION=1.2.3, so config('doccum.version') reads 1.2.3. The image itself is unchanged; the two sources are forced apart at run time.",
      "check": "container-smoke.mjs checkTopbar(). The image job failed AT THE NAMED CHECK AND NOWHERE ELSE -- the installer, the first-administrator verification and the /dashboard reach all passed, and the failure lands on the first checkTopbar call: 'container-smoke (setup) failed: version mismatch across sources -- pill: \"v1.2.3\", config('doccum.version'): \"1.2.3\", org.opencontainers.image.version label: \"9.9.9\"'. That matches, VERBATIM, the prediction recorded in the PR body before the run. THE POINT, and the reason this mutation was chosen over a simpler one: the OLD check would have passed this scenario happily, because it compared the pill against config('doccum.version') only and both read 1.2.3 -- agreeing with each other while the image was labelled something else entirely. The third source is what makes the disagreement visible at all. Run https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35376591005.",
