      "headSha": "1972fa6fec00da391c97527bfd397ce97293b607",
      "mutant": ".github/mutations.json entry `drop-move-file-subject-scoped-to-reach`, a registered guard the CI `guards` job re-runs on every push. dropMove()'s FILE SUBJECT, scoped by directory_id. Removing the whereIn leaves File::query()->find($subjectId): a file in an unreachable directory is found, abort_if does not fire, authorize('move') answers 403, and a nonexistent id still answers 404. WHICH HALF OF THE PAIR IT PROVES: only the out-of-reach test flips; the companion asserting a nonexistent id answers the same still passes with the scoping removed, because find() returns null either way and abort_if still fires. That half documents the agreement and is not the witness.",
      "check": "The `guards` job on PR #307, run https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35582497108, head 1972fa6. Verbatim:\n\n  === drop-move-file-subject-scoped-to-reach ===\n      guard present  -> \"refuses a drop of a file the viewer cannot reach\" passes\n      guard deleted  -> \"refuses a drop of a file the viewer cannot reach\" fails, as it must\n\nREAD FROM THE LOG, NOT INFERRED FROM THE JOB, and this session supplied both reasons that matters: a GREEN job does not prove a given entry ran (mutation/0037), and a RED job does not mean YOUR entry failed (decision/0111, where a green entry sat inside a red job). The run also printed \"All 99 guard(s) are load-bearing.\"",
      "verdict": "negative",
