      "mutant": ".github/mutations.json entry `drop-move-directory-subject-scoped-to-reach`, a registered guard the CI `guards` job re-runs on every push. dropMove()'s DIRECTORY SUBJECT. ITS WITNESS HAD TO BE BUILT, and that is the entry's real content: the obvious candidate -- 'refuses a folder drop from someone who may reach both ends but holds no directories.manage' -- has BOTH ENDS REACHABLE and refuses on the permission, so removing this scoping changes nothing about it. Registering it would have been an entry measuring nothing. No test dropped an unreachable FOLDER, so one was written: a member granted directories.manage directly, Manage on both ends, nothing on the dragged folder. Neither the admin (directories.view-all reaches everything) nor a plain member can express that case. WHICH HALF OF THE PAIR IT PROVES: only the out-of-reach test flips; the companion asserting a nonexistent id answers the same still passes with the scoping removed, because find() returns null either way and abort_if still fires. That half documents the agreement and is not the witness.",
      "check": "The `guards` job on PR #307, run https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35582497108, head 1972fa6. Verbatim:\n\n  === drop-move-directory-subject-scoped-to-reach ===\n      guard present  -> \"refuses a drop of a folder the viewer cannot reach\" passes\n      guard deleted  -> \"refuses a drop of a folder the viewer cannot reach\" fails, as it must\n\nREAD FROM THE LOG, NOT INFERRED FROM THE JOB, and this session supplied both reasons that matters: a GREEN job does not prove a given entry ran (mutation/0037), and a RED job does not mean YOUR entry failed (decision/0111, where a green entry sat inside a red job). The run also printed \"All 99 guard(s) are load-bearing.\"",
