      "mutant": ".github/mutations.json entry `trash-file-row-scoped-to-reach`, a registered guard the CI `guards` job re-runs on every push. trashFileRow(). The test this names was RENAMED in the same change: it read 'when the viewer may not delete it', a permission refusal, while its fixture grants nothing at all on the file's directory -- a reach case wearing a permission name. Harmless while both answered 403, misleading once they diverge. WHICH HALF OF THE PAIR IT PROVES: only the out-of-reach test flips; the companion asserting a nonexistent id answers the same still passes with the scoping removed, because find() returns null either way and abort_if still fires. That half documents the agreement and is not the witness.",
