      "headSha": "1972fa6fec00da391c97527bfd397ce97293b607",
      "mutant": ".github/mutations.json entry `preview-scoped-to-reach`, a registered guard the CI `guards` job re-runs on every push. preview(), and clause 3 with it: the docblock claimed the id was \"re-resolved against the viewer's reach\" while the lookup did none. The clause made the sentence true rather than deleting it. previewStep() routes through preview(), so the stepping path shares this guard. WHICH HALF OF THE PAIR IT PROVES: only the out-of-reach test flips; the companion asserting a nonexistent id answers the same still passes with the scoping removed, because find() returns null either way and abort_if still fires. That half documents the agreement and is not the witness.",
      "check": "The `guards` job on PR #307, run https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35582497108, head 1972fa6. Verbatim:\n\n  === preview-scoped-to-reach ===\n      guard present  -> \"refuses to preview a file the viewer cannot reach\" passes\n      guard deleted  -> \"refuses to preview a file the viewer cannot reach\" fails, as it must\n\nREAD FROM THE LOG, NOT INFERRED FROM THE JOB, and this session supplied both reasons that matters: a GREEN job does not prove a given entry ran (mutation/0037), and a RED job does not mean YOUR entry failed (decision/0111, where a green entry sat inside a red job). The run also printed \"All 99 guard(s) are load-bearing.\"",
