      "headSha": "8e63ff3b8e13c7c9b523ba70f3747d094262ef22",
      "mutant": "FilePreviewController::__invoke() used to take File $file. ONE LINE, THREE ENTRIES. viewableFileOrFail() moved up from Api\\V1\\Controller to the base controller so the three web controllers could stop using implicit model binding, and a single whereIn is the scoping for all of them. Removing it leaves File::query()->findOrFail($id) -- loadable code that finds ANY file, so an unreachable one is resolved and refused later by authorize() with 403 while a nonexistent id 404s: the oracle reopened. Three entries name the same removal with three different witnesses, because one would prove only that ONE of the three surfaces still depends on it. Only the out-of-reach half of each pair flips; the nonexistent half 404s either way (decision/0111).",
      "check": "The `guards` job on PR #315, run https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35589994265, head 8e63ff3. Verbatim:\n\n  === preview-file-scoped-to-reach ===\n      guard present  -> \"answers an unreachable file the same as a nonexistent one, for preview\" passes\n      guard deleted  -> \"answers an unreachable file the same as a nonexistent one, for preview\" fails, as it must\n\nand the closing line, \"All 103 guard(s) are load-bearing.\"",
      "verdict": "negative",
      "supersedes": null
    },
