    {
      "@id": "mutation/0047",
      "@type": "Mutation",
      "implements": [
        "item/reach-oracle-route-binding"
      ],
      "pullRequest": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/316",
      "run": "run/0021",
      "headSha": "d3eaf073b72636d5377baa5606ca7bfe18b08f3f",
      "mutant": "Browser::mount() takes a Directory resolved by IMPLICIT BINDING, so before this guard an existing directory outside the viewer's reach was found and refused by authorize() with 403 while an id no row carries 404'd from the binding. Removing the abort_if leaves authorize() as the only refusal and reopens the oracle. A REACH CHECK RATHER THAN A SCOPED LOOKUP, unlike every other entry in this family: the router resolves the model before any of our code runs, and taking ?int instead would change a signature ~105 Livewire::test() call sites pass a MODEL to, for no observable gain -- the caller sees a status and both cases answer 404 either way. THE WITNESS IS AN HTTP TEST, load-bearingly so: Livewire::test() hands mount() a resolved model, so it cannot express the nonexistent half at all.",
      "check": "The `guards` job on PR #316, run https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35590990508, head d3eaf07. Verbatim:\n\n  === files-page-directory-scoped-to-reach ===\n      guard present  -> \"answers an unreachable directory the same as a nonexistent one, for the files page\" passes\n      guard deleted  -> \"answers an unreachable directory the same as a nonexistent one, for the files page\" fails, as it must\n\nand the closing line, \"All 104 guard(s) are load-bearing.\"",
