      "run": "run/0021",
      "headSha": "d3eaf073b72636d5377baa5606ca7bfe18b08f3f",
      "mutant": "THE FIFTH SITE, the one decision/0114's predicate found after the enumeration had missed it. {archive} was an implicit binding, so another user's archive was resolved and then 403'd by abort_unless($archive->requested_by === auth()->id(), 403) while a nonexistent id 404'd -- an oracle over every archive id, leaking how many archive jobs other people have and when. THIS ENTRY REPLACES `a-directory-archive-reaches-only-its-requester`, which removed that abort_unless. decision/0111 says to repoint an entry at a test that still reaches its guard; here none can exist, because scoping the lookup to requested_by makes the abort_unless not merely unwitnessed but UNREACHABLE -- nothing the query returns can fail it. So the guard went and this entry guards what replaced it. The RULE is unchanged: still requested_by, still not the directory's policy, for every reason the controller's docblock gives. Only where it is enforced moved.",
      "check": "The `guards` job on PR #316, run https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35590990508, head d3eaf07. Verbatim:\n\n  === a-directory-archive-is-found-only-by-its-requester ===\n      guard present  -> \"hands a built archive only to the person who asked for it\" passes\n      guard deleted  -> \"hands a built archive only to the person who asked for it\" fails, as it must\n\nand the closing line, \"All 104 guard(s) are load-bearing.\"\n\nThe superseded entry's own witness is this same test, which now asserts 404 for the other user rather than 403, plus a nonexistent-id half that 404s either way.",
      "verdict": "negative",
      "supersedes": null
    },
    {
      "@id": "mutation/0049",
      "@type": "Mutation",
      "implements": [
        "item/validator-skip-guard-tested"
      ],
      "pullRequest": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/328",
      "run": "run/0021",
      "headSha": "3e56f8bfa4fc2ef24d28b813324999ce687a1bae",
      "mutant": "Deleted the env-var refusal in .github/scripts/validate-ledger.php -- the\n`if (! $witnessesMode && $mainSha === null && is_string($mainShaEnv) && $mainShaEnv !== '')`\nblock added for issue #311, 843 characters. The SECOND guard, the not-run notice, was left\nintact deliberately, so only the behaviour under test broke.\n\nReproduced locally before pushing: `MAIN_SHA=<sha> php .github/scripts/validate-ledger.php`\nexits 0 printing \"Ledger is sound\" with no \"Compared\" line -- issue #311's original defect\nrestored exactly.\n\nWHY IT WAS RUN. ledger.yml's job comment asserts \"THE LOAD-BEARING ASSERTION. Delete the\nguard in validate-ledger.php and this step exits 0 instead\". That was a claim about a\nmutation nobody had run, and CLAUDE.md is explicit that an unmutated assertion is never\ncited as evidence. Note also what this mutant does NOT witness: the notice guard, still\nintact here, is measured separately by mutation/0050.",
      "check": "The `validate-ledger.php refuses a silent skip` job on PR #328, run\nhttps://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35607810363/job/106359115050, head 3e56f8b.\nIt failed at its FIRST step, \"MAIN_SHA in the environment with no positional argument\nfails\". Verbatim:\n\n  ##[error]expected the env-var-only invocation to fail, but it exited 0 -- the\n  main-push-history check was skipped and reported as sound. Output: Note: no\n  <main-sha> argument; the main-push-history check did NOT run.\n  Ledger is sound: /home/runner/work/doccum/doccum/docs/ledger\n\nSteps 2, 3 and 4 never ran. WHICH step failed is the evidence, not that the job was red.\n\nThe mutant was narrow, which is the other half of the measurement: `validate ledger` stayed\ngreen (it uses the positional form), and all 13 jobs of tests.yml passed, `guards` and\n`image` included. One failure in the entire run, and it was the one the mutant was aimed\nat. Had a test leg also reddened, the assertion meant to be proven would still be\nunproven.",
      "verdict": "negative",
      "supersedes": null
    },
    {
      "@id": "mutation/0050",
      "@type": "Mutation",
      "implements": [
        "item/validator-skip-guard-tested"
      ],
      "pullRequest": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/329",
      "run": "run/0021",
      "headSha": "b73956dae8aca04d59874b75dfe15df4c6061514",
      "mutant": "Deleted the OTHER guard: the `if ($mainSha === null && ! $witnessesMode)` block writing\n\"Note: no <main-sha> argument; the main-push-history check did NOT run.\" to STDERR. The\nenv-var refusal was left intact this time -- the mirror image of mutation/0049.\n\nReproduced locally first: `php .github/scripts/validate-ledger.php` exits 0 printing only\n\"Ledger is sound\", so \"shape checked, history not checked\" and \"everything checked\" print\nidentically again, which is the condition issue #311's second clause was added to end. And\n`MAIN_SHA=<sha> php ...` still exits 1, confirming the untouched guard still fires.\n\nWHY A SECOND MUTATION AT ALL, and this is the point of the pair: mutation/0049 removed one\nguard of two and proved that one. Completing the item on its strength alone would have let\none witness stand for two, which is decision/0080's \"counting readers is not counting\nsources\" in mutation form -- the next reader sees \"mutated\" and stops looking.",
      "check": "The same job on PR #329, run\nhttps://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35608455992/job/106361298421, head b73956d.\nIt failed at its SECOND step, \"No sha at all still passes, but says the check did not run\":\n\n  ##[error]expected an explicit not-run notice when no <main-sha> is given, but got:\n  Ledger is sound: /home/runner/work/doccum/doccum/docs/ledger\n\nSTEP 1 PASSED, which is the load-bearing part of this result rather than an incidental\ndetail: mutation/0049 died at step 1 and this one died at step 2, so the two guards are\nmeasured by two different assertions. Had both mutants failed the same step, the pair would\nhave measured one thing twice and been recorded as two.\n\nNarrow as well: `validate ledger` green, and every test-matrix leg plus `guards` green on\nthe same run.",
      "verdict": "negative",
      "supersedes": null
    },
    {
      "@id": "mutation/0051",
      "@type": "Mutation",
      "implements": [
        "item/v1-audit"
      ],
      "pullRequest": "https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/pull/347",
      "run": "run/0021",
      "headSha": "846f232e4751803e88be68b10ada6b8408392530",
      "mutant": "PurgePeriod::handle()'s dry-run branch force-deletes the period's files before returning, while still printing the period label, the file count and the literal 'Dry run. Nothing was deleted. Pass --force to purge.' -- a dry run that purges for real and reassures you it did not.\n\nBranched off PR #346's head e65aa49 AFTER CI saw that head green at 21 of 21, per decision/0088: a differential against an unknown baseline is not a measurement.\n\nIT DELETES DIRECTLY RATHER THAN THROUGH PeriodPurger, AND THAT CHOICE IS THE DESIGN. The smoke's container configures no retention window (purge_after_years defaults to null), so PeriodPurger::blockers() reports \"No retention window is configured\" and 2019-03 is NOT purgeable. Routing the mutant through purge() would have made the command refuse and exit non-zero, failing the check at the docker exec step instead of at the row read-back -- the job would go red and the assertion under test would still be unproven. A mutant that kills the check earlier than intended measures nothing.",
      "check": "checkPurgePeriodDryRunLeavesFileInPlace()'s ROW READ-BACK, in the `image` job on PR #347 (run https://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35624263518, job\nhttps://github.com/turbophp/doccum/actions/runs/35624263518/job/106414617834, head 846f232). Read by grepping the saved job log rather than taken on report:\n\n  ##[error][setup] DoccumSmokePurgeDryRunTarget.txt is gone after a purge-period run WITHOUT\n  --force -- the dry run purged for real -- raw output: EXISTS:no WITH_TRASHED_COUNT:0\n  ##[error]container-smoke (setup) failed: purge-period dry run deleted the file it was only\n  supposed to report on\n\nTHE THREE STDOUT ASSERTIONS BEFORE IT PASSED, which is the load-bearing half of this result and not an incidental detail: their failure messages are absent from the log (grep count 0 for each of 'did not name the 2019-03 period', 'did not report 1 file for 2019-03', 'never said it deleted nothing', and '(dry run) failed'). PR #346 predicted exactly this in advance -- that the stdout checks cannot catch a silent purge because the mutant satisfies them unchanged -- and the run confirmed it rather than being read to fit it.\n\nTHE PREDICTION MISSED ONE JOB, RECORDED AS A MISS RATHER THAN RECLASSIFIED. Predicted: `image` FAIL at the read-back, the six `test` legs FAIL (ArchiveCommandsTest covers this guard twice through the test harness, an independent witness from the smoke's real binary in the shipped --no-dev image), everything else PASS. Actual: all of that, plus `lint` FAIL -- Pint's fully_qualified_strict_types rejected the inline \\App\\Models\\File:: written into the mutant. A defect in how the mutant was written, in a job independent of `image`, so it does not touch the differential; but the prediction was wrong and saying so afterwards is the only version of this record worth anything.\n\nTHE RUN URL IN THIS NODE WAS WRONG WHEN FIRST WRITTEN, and is recorded because decision/0121 is about exactly this. The first draft cited run 35623985069, a number that was not read from anywhere -- the real run is 35624263518. Caught by listing the tests runs for branch mutation/purge-dry-run-deletes before committing, which also confirmed every job conclusion quoted above: `image` failure at step 10, `lint` failure at \"Pint (format check)\", all six `test` legs failure, and `guards`, `build assets`, `release waits for the published image to boot`, `compose requires MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD`, `docs name the real image, not a placeholder` and `changelog-section.sh extracts release notes` success. Nothing in CI would have rejected the invented number.",
      "verdict": "negative",
      "supersedes": null
    },
    {
      "@id": "mutation/0052",
      "@type": "Mutation",
