      "mutant": "Deleted the `actions/checkout` step from boot-published-image. Run against a SCRATCH COPY of .github under /tmp, taken from the tree at 4723742, so the tracked tree was never dirtied -- `git status --porcelain` was empty throughout. THE JOB UNDER TEST CANNOT ITSELF BE MUTATED: release.yml's boot-published-image is guarded to a tag push and no tag exists, so it cannot be made to fail because it cannot be made to run. decision/0120's answer applies -- the mutants go against the static guard that asserts its preconditions where the project DOES run.",
      "check": "The `published image boot runs the full container smoke` check, via .github/scripts/assert-published-smoke.py, exit 1:\n\n  ::error::`boot-published-image` runs container-smoke.mjs but never checks out the repository -- `node .github/scripts/container-smoke.mjs` and `npm install --prefix .github/scripts` both read files out of the tree, so this job would fail at tag time on a path that does not exist.\n\nTHIS MUTANT EXISTS BECAUSE THE DEFECT WAS REAL. The job had no checkout at all, and the guard's first version would have passed it -- name matched, port matched, all seven variables supplied. The mutation is the regression test for a bug that shipped in the commit before it.",
