      "mutant": "Added `const NEWTHING = env('SMOKE_NEWTHING');` -- a required variable with no default -- to container-smoke.mjs, without adding it to boot-published-image's fixture step. Run against a SCRATCH COPY of .github under /tmp, taken from the tree at 4723742, so the tracked tree was never dirtied -- `git status --porcelain` was empty throughout. THE JOB UNDER TEST CANNOT ITSELF BE MUTATED: release.yml's boot-published-image is guarded to a tag push and no tag exists, so it cannot be made to fail because it cannot be made to run. decision/0120's answer applies -- the mutants go against the static guard that asserts its preconditions where the project DOES run.",
      "check": "assert-published-smoke.py exit 1, naming the variable:\n\n  ::error::`boot-published-image` never supplies SMOKE_NEWTHING, which container-smoke.mjs requires with no default and would throw on.\n\nTHIS IS WHAT MAKES THE DUPLICATED FIXTURES SAFE TO LEAVE DUPLICATED. Sharing them would mean a composite action or a reusable workflow, which would refactor the job that runs on every push. Instead the eighth required variable turns CI red on the PR that adds it, rather than silently on the next tag push -- a comment asking two lists to stay in sync is not a guard (decision/0113).",
